  "description": "redundancy.v1 §2.4, §2.14, core §3.3 (0.39): one interface entry of a descriptor, as JSON, and what the reader knows of the interface's governance (\"claim\" or \"external\": governed, with that election; \"not_governed\"; \"no_contract\": its contract not read) -> its mark and the findings. standby absent is false, token absent is true. expect.mark is \"standby\", \"serving\", or null when the entry is malformed. expect.findings, in this order: malformed (the entry not an object, or standby or token present and not a boolean, null included: core D000; nothing else is read, and it is the only finding), standby_tokenless (standby true and token false: core D012), governed_tokenless (token false, the interface governed, under either election), not_governed (standby true, the interface not governed: the mark says what core §6 says, and none of §5's questions is this profile's). Every other member of the entry is core §3.3's, and not read here."
